%I A400457 #16 Oct 18 2026 00:31:23
%S A400457 12,66,524,4866,49152,523626,5787612,65743308
%N A400457 Number of fixed polyforms with n cells in the honeycomb of the 11-faced Voronoi cell of the point (0, 0, 1/4) under space group I-43d (No. 220).
%C A400457 The cell is an 11-faced space-filling polyhedron (3^2 4^1 5^8 faces) arising as the Voronoi cell of the orbit of the point (0, 0, 1/4) under space group I-43d (No. 220); its honeycomb has 12 cell types (translation classes), each cell with 11 face-neighbors. Polyforms are face-connected clusters of cells, counted up to lattice translation only.
%C A400457 The symmetry group G of the tiling has order 24 modulo lattice translations (12 proper), and the counts satisfy the Burnside identity |G|*free(n) = Sum_g Fix_g(n).
%H A400457 Mathias Bernhard, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.07160">The Josehedron</a>, arXiv:2604.07160 [cs.CG], 2026 (method precedent; roundness benchmark).
%H A400457 Tyler Satchel Orden, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22502081">Certified space-filling polyhedra from a gated agentic search: code, certificates, catalog (MINT)</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A400457 Tyler Satchel Orden, <a href="/A400457/a400457.txt">Honeycomb adjacency and symmetry tables, with the enumeration program and run instructions</a>.
%H A400457 Moritz W. Schmitt, <a href="https://doi.org/10.17169/refubium-14374">On Space Groups and Dirichlet-Voronoi Stereohedra</a>, Dissertation, Freie Universität Berlin, 2016.
%H A400457 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_space_groups">List of space groups</a>.
%o A400457 (C++) // Redelmeier-style table-driven enumerator; see the a-file (same program as A398957).
%Y A400457 Cf. A398957, A398958, A398959 (Josehedron polyforms, same enumerator); A385028, A397707-A397709 (polyforms on other space-filler honeycombs).
